# What running this repository's own test suite leaves behind.
#
# `CONTRIBUTING.md` invites pull requests and `README.md` promises that
# `pip install -e ".[dev]" && pytest` works from a clean clone. Both were true and
# neither was tidy: the suite compiles the C example and Python writes bytecode, so a
# contributor's first `git status` after following those instructions listed files they
# did not create and could not explain — and `git add -A` before a pull request would
# have committed a 16 KB binary into a repository that ships source.
#
# WRITTEN FOR THIS PACKAGE rather than copied from the tree that generates it. That
# one ignores paths which mean nothing here and name things a reader cannot open.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Test and lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Built by the examples' own entry points when the suite exercises them. Each is the
# artefact of a `.shard/entry.sh`, which is exactly what those scripts are for — the
# manifest tells you to build in an earlier step, and here the test suite is that step.
examples/*/record
examples/*/*.o
examples/*/*.out

# What a run of Shard itself writes. `--out-dir` is where the action puts them, and a
# customer trying the quickstart against their own checkout gets them at the root.
shard-out/
shard-report.md
shard.sarif
shard_journal.jsonl
shard-telemetry.json
shard-run.log

# Credentials. Never committed, and named here so that is a property of the repository
# rather than of whoever is typing.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local agent-tooling session state. Machine-local scratch — transcripts of coding sessions against
# this checkout — and `git add -A` has already swept one of its JSON files into a commit once.
# Nothing in it belongs to the product.
#
# Contributed on this repository by hand and carried upstream on 2026-09-02 so it survives. This
# repository is GENERATED: an edit made here is replaced by the next release, so the change had to
# move into the tree the generator reads. That is why it is now in every build rather than only in
# one commit.
.opencode/
